  "nine_contiguous_BODY_formula_regions": [
    {
      "title": "Fix the actual source objects and finite-time target",
      "start": 81,
      "end": 124,
      "RAW_sha256": "93368f54378002faafb27b7c03966fc133410ef463d68f4bb55d721660076d77",
      "formula": "T_n=\\operatorname{time}(\\operatorname{record}_n),\\quad T_n=\\infty\\text{ if stopped};\\quad T_n\\le t<T_{n+1}.",
      "text": "Keep the literal source flow, reflection, hazard, first hitting time and guarded finite-record recurrence. Use the canonical Exp1 product and total NNReal thresholds. The two conclusions concern the actual half-open clock interval and the actual stored live record with finite elapsed time."
    },
    {
      "title": "Reuse initialized monotone actual clocks on the common AE event",
      "start": 125,
      "end": 137,
      "RAW_sha256": "4fb9edcb59adeeace061883b31503430e7e13bf74f66c378887d96d17fec6bde",
      "formula": "T_0=0,\\quad T_n\\le T_{n+1},\\quad\\forall t<\\infty,\\quad T_n>t\\text{ eventually}.",
      "text": "The exact finite-recursion parent supplies initialization, monotonicity and guarded next-record updates. The actual nonaccumulation parent supplies finite-horizon escape on one AE event for each fixed parameter triple. No certificate is supplied as a new public assumption."
    },
    {
      "title": "Select the predecessor of the first clock crossing",
      "start": 138,
      "end": 158,
      "RAW_sha256": "a6e6575bae7b611b201db143d38c359ddb96d7dd69f981a91cc210d0883a4ed0",
      "formula": "k=\\min\\{j:t<T_j\\}>0,\\quad n=k-1,\\quad T_n\\le t<T_{n+1}.",
      "text": "For each finite t choose the least k with t<T_k. Initialization gives k>0. Let n=k−1. Minimality gives T_n≤t, and n+1=k gives t<T_(n+1)."
    },
    {
      "title": "Prove that the half-open interval index is unique",
      "start": 159,
      "end": 167,
      "RAW_sha256": "95c372245f125826875d0c28c6e077d5b410e3e6c8d9ad85645b0a6515fccc47",
      "formula": "m>n\\Longrightarrow t<T_{n+1}\\le T_m\\le t,\\quad\\text{a contradiction}.",
      "text": "If two indices m,n satisfy their half-open inequalities, m>n would imply T_(n+1)≤T_m≤t, contradicting t<T_(n+1). The opposite inequality is symmetric. Empty zero-length intervals cause no overlap, so no extra strict-wait premise is needed."
    },
    {
      "title": "Exclude stopped records at finite covering times",
      "start": 168,
      "end": 177,
      "RAW_sha256": "0ffdb0cf396834f2fcd67bdfdc326b4dc0ff62673e1bf952aee69762e893d6d1",
      "formula": "T_n\\le t<\\infty\\Longrightarrow\\operatorname{record}_n\\ne\\mathrm{stopped}.",
      "text": "A stopped record has eventTime=∞. Its lower interval inequality ∞≤t contradicts finiteness of t. Thus every covering record must be active."
    },
    {
      "title": "Recover the actual live record and its stored time",
      "start": 178,
      "end": 186,
      "RAW_sha256": "73b4dd13e341039d38a5d971bf179dac1e8d0536e750fbaf8ca577ab051dc3fb",
      "formula": "\\operatorname{record}_n=\\mathrm{inl}(a)\\Longrightarrow T_n=a.time\\le t.",
      "text": "For an active record a the exact eventTime eliminator gives T_n=a.time. The lower interval inequality gives a.time≤t. The record supplied in the conclusion is this actual record, not a chosen external state."
    },
    {
      "title": "Keep the last live arc when the next wait is infinite",
      "start": 187,
      "end": 189,
      "RAW_sha256": "a1cf3d48f8e41c4bb605877bbd9c68dfc588ed0ad4448ae7971be6de29ac6ae2",
      "formula": "\\tau(a.state,\\varepsilon_n)=\\infty\\Longrightarrow t-a.time<\\infty=\\tau(a.state,\\varepsilon_n).",
      "text": "If the actual next waiting time is infinity, every finite NNReal elapsed offset is strictly less than it. Stopping the next jump does not erase the currently live state or invent a phase at infinity."
    },
    {
      "title": "Bound the elapsed offset for a finite next wait",
      "start": 190,
      "end": 207,
      "RAW_sha256": "fd184389bb8ad44946cbed78e3dcf2bdb9afe930bf853903e46446056e3a740a",
      "formula": "T_{n+1}=a.time+q,\\quad a.time\\le t<T_{n+1}\\Longrightarrow 0\\le t-a.time<q.",
      "text": "Write the actual finite wait as q. The existing guarded recurrence gives record_(n+1)=(a.time+q, bounce(flow(q,a.state))) and hence T_(n+1)=a.time+q. Therefore t<T_(n+1) and a.time≤t imply t−a.time<q. Subtraction is nonnegative and never evaluates an infinite elapsed duration."
    },
    {
      "title": "Prove uniqueness of the actual live record",
      "start": 208,
      "end": 210,
      "RAW_sha256": "716ab92296c3de4b6d6dd32534d2ff3c1ad0e4ae7e13f3acfa3d66f944b201a2",
      "formula": "\\mathrm{inl}(a)=\\operatorname{record}_n=\\mathrm{inl}(b)\\Longrightarrow a=b.",
      "text": "The record recursion is a function. Two live records at the same index have equal Sum.inl values, so injectivity gives equal time/state pairs. Assemble the interval and live-record conclusions on the common AE event."
    }
  ],
